Matching source for the LeJEPA fixture's natbib.sty

natbib-8.31-sources.tar.gz contains unmodified natbib 8.31 source files,
dated 2009/07/16, by Patrick W. Daly. Its LPPL grants and full license text
are retained inside. The archive includes the complete seven-file manifest
in README.v831, both upstream README files, lppl.txt and bibentry.drv.

Source distribution
https://ftp.math.utah.edu/pub/tex/historic/systems/texlive/2009/texlive2009.iso
TUG's documented historical mirror https://www.tug.org/historic/

The mirror publishes ISO SHA-256
fcd61be1ed2c82c4ac8d9ee4e5c8a7c1003ffb605d02174a35360f7c4b50644a.
Only bounded HTTPS ranges were retrieved, so Tekai did not independently
recompute the entire ISO digest. The natbib.dtx ISO member is
texmf-dist/source/latex/natbib/natbib.dtx, at bytes 2055108608 through
2055356990. Its header and README identify version 8.31. The same ISO's
generated natbib.sty matches the existing paper fixture byte-for-byte,
SHA-256 88bc70c0e48461934cab5b2accef06b74a8b3ac45ad03ccd3f2a6b7e0d6d530d.

Tekai repacked the source files on 13 October 2026 without changing their
contents. The archived form prevents the older .bst files from entering
ordinary recursive project lookup. The original paper fixture is unchanged.
To obtain the documented source and installation files, extract the archive
into a separate directory, then follow README.v831.

